(5730129, 832383, 28710, '<td valign="top">weird.<br/> <br/>I agree with the others. I mean you could easily have entered this in a free study. I mean they happen often enough right?<br/> <br/>I would say that the attitude is even a step beyond childish. Arrogant is suitable and I don''t think it would be a stretch to say it''s quite rude to everyone else who entered in the spirit of the challenge.<br/> <br/>I mean what''s the point? You just wanted to win? Why not enter yourself in the kiddie foot races at your local elementary school? You''d be guaranteed a win. OK, so that''s a pretty silly example, but is it any more childish? Or would it be more anal for the rulekeepers to DQ you from such a race on the grounds that you aren''t in the same class?<br/> <br/>I''d say that it''s a no-brainer, but whatever. Best choice at this point would be a self-DQ. But the gall that you showed in entering in knowing disregard for the guidelines for this challenge is quite offensive.</td>', 'weird. I agree with the others. I mean you could easily have entered this in a free study. I mean they happen often enough right? I would say that the attitude is even a step beyond childish. Arrogant is suitable and I don''t think it would be a stretch to say it''s quite rude to everyone else who entered in the spirit of the challenge. I mean what''s the point? You just wanted to win? Why not enter yourself in the kiddie foot races at your local elementary school? You''d be guaranteed a win. OK, so that''s a pretty silly example, but is it any more childish? Or would it be more anal for the rulekeepers to DQ you from such a race on the grounds that you aren''t in the same class? I''d say that it''s a no-brainer, but whatever. Best choice at this point would be a self-DQ. But the gall that you showed in entering in knowing disregard for the guidelines for this challenge is quite offensive.', '2009-11-17 08:29:26.000000', NULL, 0),
